🛠️ Part 6: Debugging SELinux Issues
Finding Denials
# View SELinux denials in real-time
adb logcat | grep "avc: denied"

# Example denial message:
# avc: denied { read } for pid=1234 comm="camera.provider"
#      name="video0" dev="tmpfs" ino=5678
#      scontext=u:r:example_camera_hal:s0
#      tcontext=u:object_r:video_device:s0
#      tclass=chr_file permissive=0

Reading the Denial
avc: denied { read } for pid=1234 comm="camera.provider"
              ↑           ↑            ↑
              Action      Process ID   Process name
              denied

scontext=u:r:example_camera_hal:s0
         ↑
         Source context (who tried to access)

tcontext=u:object_r:video_device:s0
         ↑
         Target context (what was being accessed)

tclass=chr_file
       ↑
       Target class (type of object)

Converting Denial to Allow Rule
# Use audit2allow tool
adb logcat -d | grep "avc: denied" | audit2allow -p device_policy

# Output:
# allow example_camera_hal video_device:chr_file read;

# Add this rule to your .te file (but verify it's appropriate!)

Verifying Labels
# Check file label
adb shell ls -Z /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.camera.provider@2.7-service.meta
# Output: u:object_r:example_camera_hal_exec:s0 /vendor/bin/hw/...

# Check process label
adb shell ps -Z | grep camera
# Output: u:r:example_camera_hal:s0 ... android.hardware.camera.provider@2.7-service.meta

# Check device label
adb shell ls -Z /dev/video0
# Output: u:object_r:video_device:s0 /dev/video0


📋 Summary Checklist
When creating SELinux policy for a HAL:
Step	File	What to Add
1	.te	Define domain type: type example_camera_hal, domain;
2	.te	Define exec type: type example_camera_hal_exec, exec_type, ...;
3	.te	Enable transition: init_daemon_domain(example_camera_hal)
4	.te	Add binder permissions: binder_use(), binder_call()
5	.te	Register as HAL: hal_server_domain()
6	.te	Add hardware access: allow ... camera_device:chr_file {...};
7	.te	Add data access: allow ... data_file:file {...};
8	.te	Add security boundaries: neverallow ...;
9	file_contexts	Label executable: 
binary u:object_r:..._exec:s0
10	file_contexts	Label data: 
.*)? u:object_r:..._data_file:s0
11	file_contexts	Label devices: 
device[0-9]+ u:object_r:..._device:s0



