📘 Topic 4: HIDL vs AIDL Differences (15 mins)
Overview Comparison
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         HIDL vs AIDL COMPARISON                              │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                              │
│   HIDL (HAL Interface Definition Language)                                  │
│   ════════════════════════════════════════                                  │
│   - Introduced: Android 8 (Oreo)                                            │
│   - Purpose: Treble HAL interfaces                                          │
│   - Transport: hwbinder (separate from system binder)                       │
│   - Status: DEPRECATED for new HALs                                         │
│                                                                              │
│   AIDL (Android Interface Definition Language)                              │
│   ═════════════════════════════════════════════                             │
│   - Introduced: Android 1.0 (for apps), Android 11 (for HALs)              │
│   - Purpose: Originally app IPC, now also HALs                              │
│   - Transport: binder (unified)                                             │
│   - Status: RECOMMENDED for new HALs                                        │
│                                                                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Detailed Comparison Table
Aspect	HIDL	AIDL (Stable)
First For HALs	Android 8	Android 11
File Extension	.hal	.aidl
Versioning	@1.0, @2.0	V1, V2
Package Format	android.hardware.camera@3.5	android.hardware.camera
Transport	hwbinder (separate)	binder (unified)
Passthrough Mode	✅ Supported	❌ Not supported
Code Generation	C++, Java	C++, Java, Rust, NDK
Memory Sharing	hidl_memory	Uses ParcelFileDescriptor
Future	Deprecated	Recommended
Syntax Comparison
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           HIDL SYNTAX (.hal)                                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                              │
│   // File: ICameraProvider.hal                                              │
│   package android.hardware.camera.provider@2.7;                             │
│                                                                              │
│   interface ICameraProvider {                                               │
│       getCameraIdList() generates (Status status, vec<string> cameraIds);  │
│                                                                              │
│       getCameraDeviceInterface(string cameraDeviceName)                     │
│           generates (Status status, ICameraDevice device);                  │
│                                                                              │
│       setCallback(ICameraProviderCallback callback)                         │
│           generates (Status status);                                        │
│   };                                                                        │
│                                                                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           AIDL SYNTAX (.aidl)                                │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                              │
│   // File: ICameraProvider.aidl                                             │
│   package android.hardware.camera.provider;                                 │
│                                                                              │
│   @VintfStability                                                           │
│   interface ICameraProvider {                                               │
│       String[] getCameraIdList();                                           │
│                                                                              │
│       ICameraDevice getCameraDeviceInterface(String cameraDeviceName);      │
│                                                                              │
│       void setCallback(ICameraProviderCallback callback);                   │
│   };                                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│   // Note: Exceptions replace status codes                                  │
│   // Note: @VintfStability marks as stable HAL interface                    │
│                                                                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Key Differences Explained
1. Versioning
HIDL:
├── android.hardware.camera.provider@2.4
├── android.hardware.camera.provider@2.5
├── android.hardware.camera.provider@2.6
└── android.hardware.camera.provider@2.7
    (Each version is separate package)

AIDL:
└── android.hardware.camera.provider
    ├── aidl_api/1/  (Version 1 frozen API)
    ├── aidl_api/2/  (Version 2 frozen API)
    └── current/     (Current development)
    (Single package, versioned via aidl_api directory)

2. Return Values & Errors
// HIDL: Status returned via callback
Return<void> getCameraIdList(getCameraIdList_cb _hidl_cb) {
    hidl_vec<hidl_string> ids = {"0", "1"};
    _hidl_cb(Status::OK, ids);  // Status in callback
    return Void();
}

// AIDL: Exceptions for errors, direct return
std::vector<std::string> getCameraIdList() {
    if (error) {
        throw ServiceSpecificException(ERROR_CODE, "Error message");
    }
    return {"0", "1"};  // Direct return
}

3. Service Registration
// HIDL Service Registration
#include <android/hardware/camera/provider/2.7/ICameraProvider.h>

sp<ICameraProvider> provider = new CameraProvider();
provider->registerAsService("internal/0");

// AIDL Service Registration
#include <aidl/android/hardware/camera/provider/ICameraProvider.h>

std::shared_ptr<ICameraProvider> provider = 
    ndk::SharedRefBase::make<CameraProvider>();
binder_status_t status = AServiceManager_addService(
    provider->asBinder().get(), 
    "android.hardware.camera.provider.ICameraProvider/internal/0");

4. Passthrough Mode (HIDL only)
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    HIDL PASSTHROUGH MODE                                     │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                              │
│   BINDERIZED (Normal):                                                      │
│   ┌─────────────┐         Binder IPC         ┌─────────────┐               │
│   │   Client    │ ◄─────────────────────────► │  HAL        │               │
│   │   Process   │      (Cross-process)       │  Process    │               │
│   └─────────────┘                             └─────────────┘               │
│                                                                              │
│   PASSTHROUGH (HIDL only):                                                  │
│   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐               │
│   │   Client Process                                         │               │
│   │   ┌───────────┐         dlopen()         ┌───────────┐  │               │
│   │   │  Client   │ ◄───────────────────────►│  HAL .so  │  │               │
│   │   │   Code    │      (Same process)      │  Library  │  │               │
│   │   └───────────┘                          └───────────┘  │               │
│   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘               │
│                                                                              │
│   Passthrough: HAL runs in client's process (faster, legacy support)       │
│   AIDL does NOT support passthrough mode!                                   │
│                                                                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

When to Use Which?
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         DECISION GUIDE                                       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                              │
│   NEW HAL? ───────────────────────────────────────────► Use AIDL            │
│                                                                              │
│   Modifying EXISTING HIDL HAL? ───────────────────────► Stay with HIDL      │
│                                                         (or migrate)         │
│                                                                              │
│   Need PASSTHROUGH mode? ─────────────────────────────► Must use HIDL       │
│                                                                              │
│   Want RUST backend? ─────────────────────────────────► Use AIDL            │
│                                                                              │
│   NDK backend needed? ────────────────────────────────► Use AIDL            │
│                                                                              │
│   Android 10 or earlier device? ──────────────────────► Use HIDL            │
│                                                                              │
│   Android 11+ device? ────────────────────────────────► Prefer AIDL         │
│                                                                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Build Configuration Comparison
# HIDL (Android.bp)
hidl_interface {
    name: "android.hardware.camera.provider@2.7",
    root: "android.hardware",
    srcs: ["ICameraProvider.hal"],
    interfaces: [
        "android.hardware.camera.device@3.5",
        "android.hardware.camera.common@1.0",
    ],
    gen_java: true,
}

# AIDL (Android.bp)
aidl_interface {
    name: "android.hardware.camera.provider",
    vendor_available: true,
    srcs: ["android/hardware/camera/provider/*.aidl"],
    stability: "vintf",
    backend: {
        cpp: { enabled: true },
        java: { enabled: true },
        ndk: { enabled: true },
        rust: { enabled: true },
    },
    versions: ["1", "2"],
}

Interview Questions
Question	Answer
HIDL vs AIDL?	HIDL is deprecated (Android 8-10), AIDL is preferred (Android 11+)
What's passthrough?	HAL runs in client process (HIDL only)
What's @VintfStability?	AIDL annotation marking interface as stable HAL
Why AIDL now?	Unified binder, Rust support, simpler syntax
Can HIDL→AIDL migrate?	Yes, Android provides migration path
