Log Priority Levels
Level	Letter	Description	When to Use
Verbose	V	Most detailed	Development only
Debug	D	Debug info	Development
Info	I	General info	Normal operation
Warning	W	Potential issues	Recoverable errors
Error	E	Errors	Failures
Fatal	F	Critical errors	Crashes
Silent	S	No output	Filter only
Basic Commands
# ============================================================================
# BASIC LOGCAT USAGE
# ============================================================================

# View all logs (live stream)
adb logcat

# View logs and exit (dump mode)
adb logcat -d

# Clear log buffer
adb logcat -c

# Clear then view new logs
adb logcat -c && adb logcat

# Save logs to file
adb logcat -d > device_logs.txt

# View logs continuously and save
adb logcat | tee device_logs.txt

Filtering Logs
# ============================================================================
# FILTERING BY TAG
# ============================================================================

# Filter by specific tag (shows only that tag)
adb logcat -s CameraService
#          ↑
#          -s means "silence all others, show only this"

# Filter by tag with priority
adb logcat -s CameraService:V
#                           ↑
#                           V = Verbose (show all levels)

# Multiple tags
adb logcat -s CameraService:V CameraProvider:D AudioFlinger:I

# Example: Camera HAL debugging
adb logcat -s ExampleCameraHAL:V ExampleCameraProvider:V ExampleCameraDevice:V

# ============================================================================
# FILTERING BY PRIORITY
# ============================================================================

# Show only Warnings and above (W, E, F)
adb logcat *:W

# Show only Errors
adb logcat *:E

# Combine tag and priority
adb logcat CameraService:V *:S
#                          ↑
#                          S = Silent (suppress everything else)

Output Formatting
# ============================================================================
